   - validate with DUNS_NUMBER_PATTERN and fdaIdentifierProblems (server/services/ectd/regulatory-identifiers.ts:203-281);
   - add the fields to the project's regulatory-identity form.
4. Extend server/services/ectd/package-identity.ts:
   - readRecordedPackageIdentity selects the new columns and returns applicantId and contact;
   - packageIdentityRefusal accepts `{ fda: true }` and refuses with PackageIdentityMissingError when the DUNS or the contact is missing or invalid.
5. Remove every `UNASSIGNED-ORG-` fallback outside dryRunPackageIdentity, using the recorded DUNS and refusing when it is absent:
   - server/routes/ectd-compile.ts:1047;
   - server/services/submission-service/submission-service.ts:2185;
   - server/services/ectd/assemble-from-core.ts:655, where exportIdentity also returns applicantId;
   - server/services/ana/AnaToolExecutor.ts:9211.
6. Thread contacts through to the packager:
   - add `contacts?: FdaApplicantContact[]` to BuildPackagerInputArgs (server/services/ectd/core-to-packager.ts:270-282) and put it into the fda block at :349-357;
   - pass it from assembleSequence and packageSequenceFromCore (assemble-from-core.ts:236-322, package-from-core.ts).
7. Telephone type:
   - add the FDA telephone-number-type code list from the vendored valid-values file to server/services/ectd/controlled-vocab/cv-v3-data.ts, with its source and checksum;
   - write `telephone-number-type` in fdaApplicantContact (regional-packager.ts:406-417) from regulatory_contact_phone_type;
   - drop the unconditional telephone gap in fdaContactGaps (:477-489) only when a code resolves.
8. Module 1 nesting. Add scripts/ectd/generate-fda-m1-headings.mjs:
   - it parses the vendored us-regional-v3-3.dtd and writes a checked-in table of {section, element, parent}, stamped with the DTD's sha256;
   - replace the context-of-use-derived SECTION_ELEMENT in fda-regional-sections.ts:16-36 with that table;
   - make fdaModule1Block emit nested parent elements, and delete the 'written directly under <m1-regional>' gap;
   - add a test that regenerates the table and fails on any diff.
9. Forms: move <form> to wherever the DTD content model puts it. If that is inside m1-1-forms, emit `<m1-1-forms><form form-type=...><leaf/></form></m1-1-forms>` and remove it from submission-information (:641). Derive form-type for 1.1 leaves from the leaf's recorded documentType through the valid-values list, refuse an unresolved one, and remove the silent `?? 'fdaft2'` default.
10. Validate us-regional.xml with xmllint --valid inside the packager, using the CAT2-01 hook.
11. Verify by failing first. Add server/services/submission-gateways/__tests__/fda-us-regional-dtd-valid.test.ts, which builds an FDA package through buildPackagerInputFromCore and runs `xmllint --valid` on m1/us/us-regional.xml. Commit its red output from HEAD (missing applicant-contacts, telephone-number-type and m1-3 nesting), then make it green.

