records.instructions:
1. Work on concept2cure-v2 only (Rule 0). Start after CAT2-01 has vendored ich-ectd-3-2.dtd.
2. Add scripts/ectd/generate-ich-headings.mjs:
   - it parses the vendored DTD's ELEMENT and ATTLIST declarations for Modules 2-5;
   - it writes server/services/submission-gateways/ectd-packager/ich-headings.generated.ts with {element, section, children, requiredAttributes, allowsLeaf}, stamped with the DTD's sha256;
   - ICH_BACKBONE in ich-headings.ts re-exports that table;
   - add a test that regenerates the table and fails on any diff;
   - delete the incorrect comment at ich-headings.ts:78-89.
3. Model the attributes per leaf with an additive migration migrations/<date>_submission_leaf_ich_heading_attributes.sql:
   - `ALTER TABLE submission_leaves ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS` for ich_substance, ich_manufacturer, ich_product_name, ich_dosage_form and ich_indication, all TEXT NULL;
   - include a Rule 1 header;
   - register it in C2C_MIGRATION_FILES before the final tenant-sweep pair, and run ci:migration-set-order and ci:migration-drop-safety;
   - mirror the columns in shared/schema/submissions.ts.
4. Carry the attributes end to end:
   - UpsertLeafInput (server/services/submission-service/submission-service.ts:2363-2385);
   - the insert (:3169-3186) and the update branch;
   - upsertLeafSchema (server/routes/submissions.ts:192-212);
   - CoreLeaf and mapCoreLeafToEctdLeaf (server/services/ectd/core-to-packager.ts);
   - EctdLeaf (ectd-packager/types.ts).
5. In the placement dialogs (client/src/concept2cure/v2/surfaces/SubmissionSeqWorkspaces.tsx, VaultPlaceIntoSubmission.tsx and AuthoringPlaceIntoFiling.tsx):
   - show the attributes the target heading requires, using requiredAttributes from the generated table;
   - prefill from regulatory_programs.product_name and regulatory_programs.indication where recorded, and never guess;
   - refuse placement until they are given, and refuse server-side too.
6. Rewrite buildIchModuleTree (ich-headings.ts:290-330):
   - group leaves by (heading element, attribute tuple), so that two drug substances emit two m3-2-s-drug-substance elements;
   - emit the escaped attributes;
   - nest each leaf under its deepest DTD heading, e.g. 3.2.S.4.1 goes to m3-2-s-drug-substance[substance, manufacturer] > m3-2-s-4-control-of-drug-substance > m3-2-s-4-1-specification;
   - throw a ValidationError when a leaf's heading is missing a required attribute.
7. Add node-extension support for content below the deepest ICH heading (for example, per-study grouping under 5.3.5.1), only where the DTD permits it.
8. Replace the ctdFolderSlug use in leafPackagePath (regional-packager.ts ~:185-209) with the ICH folder-name table (for example m3/32-body-data/32s-drug-sub/<substance-manufacturer>/32s4-contr-drug-sub/32s41-spec/), sourced from the ICH specification and pinned by test. Prior sequences keep the hrefs recorded in their manifests; lifecycle uses leaf IDs.
9. Validate index.xml with xmllint --valid in the packager, using the CAT2-01 hook, and update server/services/ectd/qualification/golden-fixtures.ts with the attributes.
10. Verify by failing first. Add a test that packages the golden fixture with leaves at 3.2.S.4.1, 3.2.P.5.1, 4.2.3.2 and 5.3.5.1 and runs `xmllint --valid index.xml`. Commit its red output from HEAD (missing required attributes), then make it green.

records.humanTestingNote:
This hits any tester who places a nonclinical or clinical study report (e.g. 4.2.3.2 or 5.3.5.1) into an FDA sequence and then compiles, freezes or dispatches it. They get 'FDA validation 1789 (technical rejection): N file(s) in Module 4/5 study sections would be referenced by no Study Tagging File … Give each its study id and STF file-tag', and no field anywhere in the Submission Center lets them do that. Workarounds:
- test FDA sequences only with Module 1-3 leaves or leaves at 4.3, 5.2, 5.3.6 or 5.4;
- on staging, set submission_leaves.study_id and stf_file_tag directly in the database;
- use AnA's package_ectd_for_region tool, which builds a package outside the sequence path.

